<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sluys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24 June <a href="/years/1340">1340</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · <a href="/today-in-history/june-24">On this day: 24 June</a> · Also known as Battle of l'Écluse · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sluys was a naval battle fought on 24 June 1340 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwin">Zwin</a> estuary off Sluis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, early in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. The English fleet of Edward III attacked the French fleet assembled for an invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and destroyed it almost entirely. The victory gave England control of the Channel for years and allowed its armies to land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sluys.jpg" alt="Battle of Sluys" width="320" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BattleofSluys.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Hundred Years’ War the English fleet destroyed the French navy at the <b>Battle of Sluys</b> off the Flemish coast in 1340, and in later centuries southern Flanders was repeatedly fought over by France and Spain.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-flanders">County of Flanders · Military</a></li></ul></section>
